                                "sense_id": "74761e35-cd81-35c3-bee5-16cb1b8c4fd8",
                                "text": "Actor serialization […]might even lead to possible deadlock. To mitigate that risk, there's an important exception to actor serialization: actors are reentrant. This means that when an actor itself says await, then while the actor's code is waiting, its members can be accessed from outside the actor using await."
